{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Eat</b> — an imperative, meaning eat honey, but much is not good, for the proper eating of honey is good." "<b>and search out their glory</b> — that of the righteous, it is glory to search out. And its meaning is that one should search out their wisdom, which is their glory and their splendor. And behold, this is proper eating of honey, as it were. And like it: 'Eat, my son, honey, for it is good,' and written after it: 'so is knowledge.' [The passage quotes Proverbs 24:13–14.]"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:47.197239815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}